---
layout: base.njk
title: "DPRK Repo Scanner"
description: "Repository indicators for BeaverTail, InvisibleFerret and OtterCookie: the searchable ruleset and PolinRider affected-repository list, the latest GitHub scan results, and how the Contagious Interview and PolinRider delivery vectors work."
permalink: "/repo-scanner/"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
extra_head: '<script src="/assets/js/ioc-search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/js/table-filter.js" defer></script>'
---
{#
  src/repo-scanner/index.njk: the repository-indicator search (ioc-search.js
  with data-ioc-index, emitted by src/repo-scanner-index.njk), the latest GitHub
  scan, and the two delivery vectors. /repo-scanner/results/ redirects to
  #scan-results.
#}
{% set scan = scanResults.latest %}
{% set polinriderDataset = iocs["polinrider-affected-repos"][0] %}
{% set repo = iocIndex.repo_scanner %}

<section>
  <h1>DPRK Repo Scanner</h1>
  <p>
    DPRK-linked operators deliver <strong>BeaverTail</strong>,
    <strong>InvisibleFerret</strong> and <strong>OtterCookie</strong> through
    source repositories: in a coding assessment sent during a staged job
    interview, and as code injected into legitimate repositories. This page
    holds the indicators for both and the latest GitHub scan.
  </p>
  {% set disclaimer = {
    title: "Leads, not verdicts",
    body: 'A match here means a report associated the value with these campaigns, or GitHub search found the string in a public repository. It does not show that a repository or its author is malicious or DPRK-linked: strings coincide with legitimate code, and a repository on the PolinRider list is almost always a victim. See the <a href="/sources/#sourcing-methodology">sourcing methodology</a>.'
  } %}{% include "partials/disclaimer.njk" %}
</section>

<section id="repository-indicators">
  <h2>Search repository indicators</h2>
  <p>
    {{ repo.total | thousands }} indicators: the curated ruleset, each entry
    cited to its report, and {{ polinriderDataset.entry_count | thousands }}
    repositories
    {% set externalLink = { url: polinriderDataset.source.url, text: "OpenSourceMalware", sameTab: true } %}{% include "partials/external-link.njk" %}
    reports as compromised by PolinRider as of {{ polinriderDataset.source.date }}.
    Neither is in the <a href="/remote-workers/">Remote Workers</a> index.
  </p>

  <div class="ioc-search" hidden data-ioc-search data-ioc-index="/assets/data/repo-scanner-index.json">
    {% set searchBox = { id: "ioc-search-input", label: "Search repository indicators", placeholder: "Repository owner or name, package name, filename, domain, or wallet address", count: "data-ioc-count" } %}{% include "partials/search-box.njk" %}
    {% set filterChips = { dimension: "type", short: "Type", label: "Filter by indicator type", allLabel: "All types (" + (repo.total | thousands) + ")", counts: repo.counts_by_type, formatValue: "replace-underscore" } %}
    {% include "partials/filter-chips.njk" %}
    {% set filterChips = { dimension: "campaign", short: "Cluster", label: "Filter by DPRK activity cluster", allLabel: "All clusters", counts: repo.counts_by_campaign } %}
    {% include "partials/filter-chips.njk" %}
    {% include "partials/ioc-download-controls.njk" %}
  </div>

  {% set iocTable = { results: true } %}{% include "partials/ioc-table.njk" %}

  {% include "partials/show-more.njk" %}

  <noscript>
    <p class="form-hint">
      Searching requires JavaScript. The {{ repo.recent | length }} most recent
      indicators are listed below; the full set is available as
      <a href="/assets/data/repo-scanner-index.json">JSON</a> and under
      <a href="/indicators/browse/">Browse indicators</a>.
    </p>
  </noscript>

  {% set iocTable = { records: repo.recent } %}{% include "partials/ioc-table.njk" %}
</section>

<section id="scan-results">
  <h2>Latest GitHub scan</h2>
  <p>
    Runs are started by hand; this is the last run, not a live feed.
    {% if scan.ran_at %}
    It finished on {{ scan.ran_at | truncate(10, true, "") }} against
    {{ scan.ruleset_version }}, ran
    {{ (scan.query_count or scan.queries_executed | length) | thousands }} queries and recorded
    {{ scan.matches | length | thousands }} matches.
    {% else %}
    No scan has been run yet.
    {% endif %}
    A row tagged <span class="tag-chip">detection or research repository</span>
    matched in a repository that appears to publish detection rules.
  </p>
  {% if scan.status == "no_scan_run_yet" and scan.notes %}
  <p><em>{{ scan.notes }}</em></p>
  {% endif %}
  {% set scannedEntries = scan.ruleset_version | rulesetEntryCount %}
  {% set liveEntries = iocs["repo-scan-ruleset"] | length %}
  {% if scannedEntries and liveEntries > scannedEntries %}
  <p class="form-hint">
    The last run searched for {{ scannedEntries | thousands }} of
    {{ liveEntries | thousands }} ruleset entries.
  </p>
  {% endif %}

  {% if scan.matches and scan.matches.length > 0 %}
  {% set tableFilter = { target: "#scan-matches-table", noun: "matches", page: limits.list, id: "scan-search-input", label: "Search scan matches", placeholder: "Indicator id, package name, repository, or file path" } %}
  {% include "partials/table-filter.njk" %}
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="results-table results-table--scan" id="scan-matches-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Matched IOC</th>
          <th scope="col">Location</th>
          <th scope="col">Matched at</th>
          <th scope="col">Context</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for match in scan.matches %}
        {% set matchKind = match.kind or (match | scanMatchKind) %}
        <tr>
          <td><code>{{ match.ioc_id }}</code><br>{{ match.matched_value }}</td>
          <td>{% set externalLink = { url: match.location, text: match.location | githubLocationLabel, rel: "noopener noreferrer nofollow", sameTab: true } %}{% include "partials/external-link.njk" %}</td>
          <td class="cell-date">{{ match.matched_at | truncate(10, true, "") }}</td>
          <td>
            {{ match.context }}
            {% if matchKind == "research" %}
            <span class="tag-chip">detection or research repository</span>
            {% endif %}
          </td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  {% include "partials/table-filter-more.njk" %}
  {% else %}
  <p>No matches recorded in the latest scan.</p>
  {% endif %}

  {% if scan.status_note %}
  <details class="disclosure">
    <summary>Run notes</summary>
    <p>{{ scan.status_note }}</p>
    <p><strong>Scan ID:</strong> <code>{{ scan.scan_id }}</code></p>
  </details>
  {% endif %}

  {% if scan.queries_executed and scan.queries_executed.length > 0 %}
  <details class="disclosure">
    <summary>Queries executed ({{ (scan.query_count or scan.queries_executed | length) | thousands }})</summary>
    <p>Every query the scan ran, then a count of package matches dropped as non-exact dependencies:</p>
    <pre class="query-block">{% for q in scan.queries_executed %}{{ q }}
{% endfor %}</pre>
  </details>
  {% endif %}

  {% if scanResults.history and scanResults.history.length > 0 %}
  <details class="disclosure">
    <summary id="scan-history">Scan history ({{ scanResults.history.length }} run{% if scanResults.history.length != 1 %}s{% endif %})</summary>
    <p>Most recent first.</p>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="results-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Ran at</th>
            <th scope="col">Mode</th>
            <th scope="col">Ruleset version</th>
            <th scope="col">Queries</th>
            <th scope="col">Matches</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for run in scanResults.history %}
          <tr>
            <td>{{ run.ran_at | truncate(10, true, "") }}</td>
            <td>{{ run.mode }}</td>
            <td>{{ run.ruleset_version }}</td>
            <td>{{ run.query_count }}</td>
            <td>{{ run.match_count }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </details>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section id="contagious-interview">
  <h2>Contagious Interview</h2>
  <p>
    Contagious Interview is the public name for fake recruiters who send a
    developer a coding assessment as a repository. Running it pulls BeaverTail,
    a JavaScript infostealer that typically fetches the InvisibleFerret
    backdoor, with OtterCookie increasingly in the same chains. A September 2026
    joint advisory from Japan&rsquo;s National Police Agency, the FBI and
    partners put its reach since late 2025 at some thirty thousand infected
    devices.
  </p>
</section>

<section id="polinrider">
  <h2>The PolinRider vector</h2>
  <p>
    {% set externalLink = { url: "https://github.com/OpenSourceMalware/PolinRider", text: "PolinRider" } %}{% include "partials/external-link.njk" %},
    documented by OpenSourceMalware, injects malicious code into rarely audited
    configuration files such as <code>postcss.config.mjs</code> in legitimate
    repositories, reached through compromised maintainer accounts, pull requests
    and dependencies. The payload is BeaverTail. {{ polinriderDataset.entry_count | thousands }}
    repositories are affected, most of them victims; they are listed under the
    <a href="/repo-scanner/?cluster=PolinRider#repository-indicators">PolinRider</a>
    cluster above.
  </p>
</section>

<section id="how-the-scanner-works">
  <h2>How the scanner works</h2>
  <p>
    The scanner is a hunting aid, not a verdict engine. It turns the ruleset
    into GitHub code-search queries (the <a href="#scan-results">latest scan</a>),
    and a person reviews every match before anything is published.
  </p>
</section>
